# The den tree PAX carries as /bin/den, with /bin/git a symbolic link to
# den (px90; tools/mkden builds it, tools/install-den installs it).
#
# den is version control in wolf (wolffe-lang/den, Track 16), reading and
# writing Git's repository formats byte for byte: the same object ids,
# trees, commits, tags, index, refs, packed-refs, reflogs and config as
# Git 2.56.0, its black-box oracle. Its clean room is Git's: Git's
# documentation, published specifications and black-box runs of the
# pinned git only, never Git's source, libgit2 or another VCS's code
# (den's README, "Clean room"). den is public; pax has no reason to read
# its source beyond what building it needs.
#
# den trunk at the time of px90 (2026-11-03): 13bc2caa (r41p's pin of den
# to wolf 0.2.36), pinned in its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.36 /
# lupin 0.1.58 / wolf-std 78b9d3cb. tools/mkden builds it with THAT
# toolchain, not with kernel/wolf.pin's, as the scent, lope and aspen
# builders build theirs, through den's own tools/mkden, twice, refusing
# two digests.
#
# What the pin carries: den's M0-M4, every local verb. Objects and
# plumbing (init, hash-object, cat-file, mktree, commit-tree, mktag); the
# index and the worktree (add, rm, mv, status, commit -m/-F/-a/--amend,
# restore, checkout of paths); diff and history (diff, log, show);
# refs (branch, tag, switch, reset); merge, revert, cherry-pick and linear
# rebase within den's measured limits; blame; stash; notes; packs
# (pack-objects, verify-pack, count-objects, fsck --full, repack,
# prune-packed).
#
# What it lacked at px90's pin: the wire (clone, fetch, pull, push: den#39,
# M5), HTTPS, hooks, a config writer (`config --get` only), `gc`, and an
# editor: a requested editor is never launched, so a message comes from -m
# or -F. den did not read argv[0] at that pin, so `git` answered exactly as
# `den` does, `--version` included.
#
# The static binary depends on the libc.a it links: built in the
# baseline Ubuntu 24.04 container (glibc 2.39-0ubuntu8.9), never on
# kasumi's CachyOS glibc; px90's sums are in notes/px90-den-on-pax.md.
DEN_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/den
# px90 (2026-11-03): den trunk, r41p's pin to wolf 0.2.36; M0-M4.
# px97 (2026-11-04): den trunk 584b18a, 139 commits after 13bc2ca, the same
# toolchain (wolf 0.2.36 / lupin 0.1.58 / wolf-std 78b9d3cb). It adds M5's
# wire within its limits (clone, explicit and configured fetch, pull by
# merge or rebase, push with leases, upload-pack, receive-pack and a
# one-session loopback daemon over file://, git:// and SSH) and the bounded
# config edits `remote add/remove/rename/set-url` and `branch
# --set-upstream-to`; `config` itself is still `--get` only, and HTTPS,
# hooks, `gc` and an editor are still absent. tests/mpx5-den types the
# local verbs only, as at px90.
DEN_REV=584b18a35fe7373735b673601af71e1722f5af29
